**The engine calls the mod's Lua to run trade, and it does so on a worker thread.** One caller, 0x27B1A2, inside 0x27B160, which is the per-country body of ProcessAITradeFunctor - and FINDINGS-tick has that functor fanned out from RunHourlyPass at 0x6829DC, every hour. So this is **once per country per hour, on a TBB worker thread**.

It draws MT19937Next (0x6A2B90) directly against the game state's generator at +0x124 - not through Random (0x6A2F80) - and:

    if (draw % 6 == 0)        Lua ProposeTrades(country->ai (+0x1D8), country->tag (+0xCA4))
    else if (draw % 10 == 0)  Lua EvalutateExistingTrades(country->ai, country->tag)

The bridge is 0x110280 with the function name in EAX and a result buffer in ESI. Both names are BlackICE's own, in `script/ai_trade.lua` (`EvalutateExistingTrades` is misspelled in the engine's literal too, so the mod's spelling is required). **So the AI's trade-route decisions are entirely the mod's**, and a script error there silently stops the AI trading.

**Before that, the player's trade offers under automate_trade** (0x4DC4A6-0x4DC66B, read 2026-10-13): only for the local player's own country (GetLocalPlayer()+0x24 == the country's id), with automate_trade set (+0x34) and foreign policy not delegated (+0x38 flag 0 != 1). For each pending PROPOSE whose slot 18 is true it asks GetAIAcceptance (slot 17); a non-trade is kept unanswered for CEU3Idler::Update; a trade is rolled with **a private C-runtime rand() seeded to 1 at every call** - x = x*214013 + 2531011, r = (x>>16) & 0x7FFF, two draws, roll = (r1*r2) % 100 - accepted when roll < score (the first only; later accepted trades are kept), else declined, each answer posted through MakeCommand. Actions failing slot 18 or not PROPOSE are dropped. Then RetainPendingDiplomaticActions. Because the seed is reset every hour, the rolls are the same fixed sequence each time: 47, 0, 56, 24, 68, 25, 87, 51...
